# claudeSSSF environment. Copy to .env at the target repo root.
#
# THE DEFAULT ROSTER NEEDS NO KEYS AT ALL.
# Every agent runs on `coding_agent: claude_code`, which shells out to the
# `claude` CLI on your machine. That CLI is already signed in to your Claude
# subscription, so the factory spends your plan's allowance and there is
# nothing to fill in below.
#
# Check you are signed in: `claude --version`, then run `claude` once
# interactively.
#
# YOU ONLY NEED A KEY IF YOU SWITCH AN AGENT TO PI.
# Set `coding_agent: pi` on an agent and its `model:` becomes a provider/model-id
# pattern; the provider half decides which key must be set, and which key pi
# reads for that provider comes from ~/.pi/agent/models.json.
#
#   google/gemini-3.6-flash                      served via openrouter -> OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#   fireworks/accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3  fireworks             -> FIREWORKS_API_KEY
#   openai/gpt-5.6-terra                         openai                -> OPENAI_API_KEY
#
# Nothing validates this for you. `agents.validate()` checks that a model is
# written in its interface's vocabulary, not that the provider is reachable or
# that its key is set, so a missing key shows up when that agent runs.

# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# FIREWORKS_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides
# CC_PATH=                         # claude binary if not on PATH, or to pin a build.
#                                  # On Windows the resolver prefers the native
#                                  # claude.exe over npm's .CMD shim on purpose:
#                                  # cmd.exe truncates argv at the first newline,
#                                  # which would silently cut the system prompt
#                                  # down to its first line.
# CC_PERMISSION_MODE=              # default bypassPermissions. The agent acts
#                                  # freely and permissions.py rolls back any
#                                  # write outside its `writes:` boundary.
#                                  # Set acceptEdits for a narrower blast radius.
# PI_PATH=pi                       # pi binary, only for coding_agent: pi agents
# PI_MODELS_PATH=~/.pi/agent/models.json
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name
